  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1) \nHot conditions are expected the next several days. Continued the heat\nadvisory through Thursday. There is the potential that some areas\nsouth of Dayton to Columbus will reach criteria on Friday, however\nwith this being further out in time and with convective coverage\nuncertainties held off on any advisory expansion and kept mention in\nthe HWO. Tomorrow has the best chance of more widespread heat \nadvisory criteria as precipitation coverage will be more limited. \nThursday there is greater confidence in heat advisory across the \nsouth than northern portions of the region due to greater \nthunderstorm potential across the north.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2)\nShowers and thunderstorms have been present across northern portions\nof the region most of the day. NBM has been struggling to pick up on\nprecipitation signatures and therefore have made several changes to\nprecipitation chances through Friday. Expect Wednesday to be more\nlimited in precipitation chances with just a slight chance across\nnorthern portions of the area. There are much better chances Thursday\nespecially in the afternoon and into the evening hours, however\nthunderstorm chances will continue into Thursday night. Additional\nthunderstorms will develop on Friday especially across west central\nOhio southeastward to the lower Scioto River valley. There will be\nthe potential for severe weather both days. Locally heavy rainfall\nwill also be possible and will have the potential for isolated\nflooding if multiple storms move over the same area. Active weather\ncontinues for Saturday. Sunday will have less coverage, however\ncannot rule out isolated showers and thunderstorms around the Tri-\nState Sunday evening. There is more uncertainty in precipitation \nchances going into early next week.",
